    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the established pattern in this codebase exactly. `Owner` already hosts a family of `@Transient` derived getters \u2014 `getDisplayName()`, `getInitials()`, `getMembershipNumber()`, `getMembershipLevel()`, `getLocality()`, `isBulkSignupWarning()` \u2014 each with the same Javadoc shape (\"Not persisted \u2014 derived from \u2026\"). `getContactPreference()` slots in right beside them, uses the same idiom, and is placed logically (after the other derived accessors). The OpenAPI schema entry mirrors the sibling `bulkSignupWarning` property (title/description/`readOnly: true`).\n\nOne thing I considered and deliberately am not flagging: the `hasEmail` expression (`this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank()`) is duplicated verbatim from `getMembershipLevel()`. Extracting a private `hasEmail()` helper would be a defensible cleanup, but the existing code already inlines that exact check in `getMembershipLevel()`, so inlining it again is the *consistent* choice here \u2014 introducing a helper for just this method (without also refactoring `getMembershipLevel`) would be less coherent than matching the surrounding idiom. The derived logic lives in the right unit (the entity, alongside its peers), nothing is a catch-all, and a maintainer would find this entirely natural.",
